# matrix/inventory/hosts -- the inventory for matrix-docker-ansible-deploy (MDAD)
#
# What it is:
#   MDAD (https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy) is a large, community
#   maintained Ansible playbook that installs a complete Matrix server: Synapse, PostgreSQL,
#   Traefik, Element Web, LiveKit for calls and dozens of optional services, all as Docker
#   containers managed by systemd. This lab does not copy that playbook into the repository; it
#   pins one exact version (a git commit) and gives it OUR configuration: this inventory and
#   host_vars/matrix.lab.internal/vars.yml. That is the usual way to consume a third-party
#   playbook: upstream code stays upstream, your configuration stays in your repository.
#
# Where it is used:
#   ansible/playbooks/matrix-prepare.yml copies this folder into ~/mdad/inventory/ on
#   ansible-control (MDAD expects its inventory there, and ignores that folder in git).
#   scripts/Deploy-LabMatrix.ps1 then runs MDAD there. Edit the files here, not on the VM.
#
# The group name "matrix_servers" is what MDAD's playbook targets. The host's inventory name
# matrix.lab.internal follows MDAD's convention (the homeserver's FQDN); it selects the folder
# host_vars/matrix.lab.internal/. The machine is the lab VM "matrix", reached by its DNS name
# (ansible_host; inside the lab it resolves to the VM's own address 10.10.10.30), as user
# "ansible" with the lab key (~/.ssh/id_ed25519 on ansible-control, ssh's default key file) and
# sudo (become) to root.
#
# Note: keep comments on their own lines (see ansible/inventory/hosts.ini).

[matrix_servers]
matrix.lab.internal ansible_host=matrix.lab.internal ansible_user=ansible ansible_become=true ansible_become_user=root
